ivers, other optical and optoelectronic devices, modules, and systems worldwide. Its products include critical components consisting of detectors, passive optics, thermal solutions, and PICS; silicon photonics and other advanced optical technologies; and coherent transmission components, transport products, optical amplifiers, passive optical components, optical line systems, and multi-rail platform. The company's Datacenter and Communications segment offers transceivers, co-packaged optics, and optical circuit switches, as well as other systems, such as subsystems, modules, and semiconductor devices for datacenter and communications applications; and VCSELS, EELS, pump lasers, and other components, optics, and ICs for datacenter and communication applications. Its Industrial segment offers excimer lasers, solid-state lasers, and CO2 lasers; laser systems for various industrial applications, including semiconductor capital equipment, display manufacturing, precision manufacturing, and scientific research; and laser systems and subsystems comprising high-power lasers for materials processing. This segment also provides engineered materials, laser optics, thermoelectric components, and advanced ceramic and metal-matrix composite materials and products. It markets its products and services through a direct sales force, representatives, and distributors. The company was formerly known as II-VI Incorporated and changed its name to Coherent Corp. in September 2022. Coherent Corp. was incorporated in 1971 and is headquartered in Saxonburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Robert Anderson | CEO, President & Employee Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 51K people. Revenue per employee of $138K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, improving at 19%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 33\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Coherent Corp. is a large-cap technology business with a $38.0B market cap on $7.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.5\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 5.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 864% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.63715830020295},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"COHR vs. NPO: Which Stock Is the Better Value Option?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025757/cohr-vs-npo-which-stock-is-the-better-value-option?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3025757","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793979604.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Coherent (COHR) Stock Price Falls As Q1 Earnings Fuel Valuation Debate","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nyse-cohr/coherent/news/coherent-cohr-stock-price-falls-as-q1-earnings-fuel-valuatio","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793925607.261,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Coherent Corp (COHR) (Q1 2027) Earnings Call Highlights: Record $2. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/coherent-corp-cohr-q1-2027-210806528.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793912886.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.727,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Coherent Surges 13% as Investors Revisit $20 Billion AI Deal After Sell-Off; Lumentum Climbs 4%, Applied Optoelectronics Gains 3%","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/coherent-surges-13-investors-revisit-191027000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992523.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"ti