,"In past sell-offs it fell 44% in the 2020 crash, 60% in the 2022 bear market and 68% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $20.01 (margin of safety -864%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 45%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: P/E 39.9 vs 26.7 and EV/EBITDA 21.9 vs 16.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 32% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -2.7% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 25 covering analysts target $388 on average, 101% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 2% falls short of the cost of capital of 12.2%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.62).","It burns cash (FCF margin -14%).","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.10x.","ROE of 7% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 10.2% of revenue on R&D and 2.6% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.8x net debt to EBITDA ($2.0B of cash against $3.2B of debt), with interest covered 5.5x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.43).","Working capital ties up about 124 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 11.3% over 3 years and 24.0% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 32%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 2.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 12%.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (15.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.4%, and institutions hold 89%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $4.9M sold).","Net share issuance leaves shareholder yield negative (-5.3%), diluting holders.","The share count has grown 13.2% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 51,478 employees, each generates about $138K of revenue, 0.4x the Technology median, and productivity has risen 19.3% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$20K per employee.","CEO pay is $4.6M (33x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":43,"head":"Avoid: priced 864% above its fair value of $20.01.","pros":["Revenue grew 11.3%/yr over 3y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.8x","Altman Z in the safe zone","25 analysts' mean target $388 (+101%)","12-1 month momentum +112%"],"cons":["Trades 864% above fair value of $20.01","ROIC 2.1% vs WACC 12.2%","FCF margin 14.4% (burns cash)","P/E 39.9x vs sector 26.7x","EV/EBITDA 21.9x vs sector 16.4x"],"flags":["Priced 864% above its fair value of $20.01","Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash"],"need":[],"buy_below":17.01,"vc":{"base":20.01,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":20.01,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.4543,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"COHR","date":"2026-11-06"}